  "notes": "West leads the ♦J against 5♣. If West's diamond lead is a singleton the contract will have no chance. Even if the ♦J is from a doubleton there is not much hope.\n\nEast will have to have a doubleton ♣K. South will have to get to dummy and at the same time not allow a trump promotion via diamond plays from East.\n\nIf South plays low from dummy at trick 1 East will duck. South will need to get to dummy in hearts. The defense will win the ♥A and play a second diamond, won by East. A further diamond lead will promote a trump trick.\n\nSouth's only (slim) hope is to play the ♦Q at trick 1. If East ducks, maintaining defensive communications, South will have his dummy entry and be able to draw trump. If East wins the ♦A the link between the defenders' hands will have been severed. As long as West has the ♥A, South will be able to get to the dummy in hearts to play trumps.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦J against 5♣. If West's diamond lead is a singleton the contract will have no chance. Even if the ♦J is from a doubleton there is not much hope.",
    "East will have to have a doubleton ♣K. South will have to get to dummy and at the same time not allow a trump promotion via diamond plays from East.",
    "If South plays low from dummy at trick 1 East will duck. South will need to get to dummy in hearts. The defense will win the ♥A and play a second diamond, won by East. A further diamond lead will promote a trump trick.",
    "South's only (slim) hope is to play the ♦Q at trick 1. If East ducks, maintaining defensive communications, South will have his dummy entry and be able to draw trump. If East wins the ♦A the link between the defenders' hands will have been severed. As long as West has the ♥A, South will be able to get to the dummy in hearts to play trumps."
  ],
